l":"https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas","homepage":"https://pandas.pydata.org","size":378810,"stargazers_count":47298,"watchers_count":47298,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":19393,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3594,"license":{"key":"bsd-3-clause","name":"BSD 3-Clause \"New\" or \"Revised\" License","spdx_id":"BSD-3-Clause","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/bsd-3-clause","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTU="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["alignment","data-analysis","data-science","flexible","pandas","python"],"visibility":"public","forks":19393,"open_issues":3594,"watchers":47298,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/pulls/19330","html_url":"https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/pull/19330","diff_url":"https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/pull/19330.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/pull/19330.patch","merged_at":"2018-01-27T16:55:23Z"},"body":"- [x] closes #19157 \r\n- [x] tests added / passed\r\n- [x] passes `git diff upstream/master -u -- \"*.py\" | flake8 --diff`\r\n- [x] whatsnew entry\r\n\r\nThis issue is due to self._init_dict({0: values}, index, columns, dtype=dtype) will call for the filtering if columns passed (`data = {k: v for k, v in compat.iteritems(data) if k in columns}`), see function ``_init_dict`` of [frame.py](https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/blob/master/pandas/core/frame.py) \r\n\r\nSo `self._init_dict({0: values}, index, columns, dtype=dtype)` expects the column name of values as '0', but since we pass a column with a different name, upon filtering it will result in an empty DataFrame. \r\n\r\nMy solution assumes that the conversion of a series of DatetimeIndex with tz_info. Hence, we will initialize a DataFrame according to the given column name. If no column name specified, index '0' is chosen. I introduced an assertion to warn the users if multiple column names are passed.\r\n\r\nUpdate 27-01-2018: The updated PR includes a test, and update on whatsnew entry. The revised solution uses ``_arrays_to_mgr`` instead, such that a default column name 0 is specified if ``columns`` not specified.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/19330/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/19330/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/comments/359251673","html_url":"https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/19157#issuecomment-359251673","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/19157","id":359251673,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM1OTI1MTY3Mw==","user":{"login":"JQGoh","id":8138573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMzg1NzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8138573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JQGoh","html_url":"https://github.com/JQGoh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JQGoh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JQGoh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JQGoh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JQGoh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JQGoh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JQGoh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JQGoh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JQGoh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JQGoh/received_events","type":"Use